#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:107
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Attach the impact report to the re-pin: the changes that reach this site (only what it mounts), and its own files that look like adaptations of a changed file. The team adds what a diff cannot see: which policies, local decisions and translations rest on the changed text."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:106
#. Diagram label
msgid "Compare old, new and our adaptations"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:123
#. Diagram label
msgid "Decide each adaptation: keep, revise or retire"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:112
#. Diagram label
msgid "Does the change touch an adaptation or policy?"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:135
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Each revision is an ordinary content change, reviewed on its staging preview through content change review, on the re-pin&#x27;s branch or a branch that merges with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:153
#. Diagram label
msgid "Every layer current with the new version"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:154
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Every site in the cone has moved, and each adaptation has a recorded decision."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:100
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "For each site that is ready now, open one re-pin pull request that moves its pins from the old version to the new one. Its staging preview is a full build with QA. A site&#x27;s standing consent may let its own workflow open this pull request."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:51
#. Diagram label
msgid "Guideline publisher"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:35
#. Diagram label
msgid "Guideline Updates"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:33
#. Diagram label
msgid "Guideline Updates: take up a new version, layer by layer, with a review of every adaptation"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:92
#. Diagram label
msgid "Map the affected layers in order"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:140
#. Diagram label
msgid "Merge the re-pin with its decided revisions"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:148
#. Diagram label
msgid "More layers left to re-pin?"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:57
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Moves the pins, one layer at a time and in dependency order, so each site re-pins only after every layer it takes from has landed. Each re-pin is a pull request with a staging preview and the impact report attached. In rapid development this lane runs on its own for changes that touch no adaptation."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:164
#. Diagram label
msgid "no"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:124
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "One recorded decision per affected adaptation, with its reason: keep it as is, revise it to the new version, or retire it because the new version now covers it. A decision to diverge from the new version is recorded as such."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:99
#. Diagram label
msgid "Open the re-pin for the next ready layer"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:82
#. Diagram label
msgid "Publish the version with its change notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:89
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Rapid development: a lower layer merged a change, and the sites above it need the new pin. The same steps run, and most such changes take the technical path only."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:56
#. Diagram label
msgid "Re-pin steward and build pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:117
#. Diagram label
msgid "Review the impact with stakeholders"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:134
#. Diagram label
msgid "Revise the adaptations as decided"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:93
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Run the re-pin planner (mount:repin:cone) with the fleet and the changed repository. It lists every site downstream in waves, so a site moves only after the layers it takes from have moved, and marks which sites are ready now."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:36
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Taking up a new version of a guideline, or a changed lower layer, is a re-pin and a review at once. The steward maps the affected layers and re-pins them in dependency order. For each re-pin, the adaptation team compares the old version, the new version and its own adaptations. A change that touches no adaptation or policy merges on the technical path. One that does goes to the adaptation committee, which decides for each adaptation whether to keep, revise or retire it. Revisions are ordinary content changes (Process_ContentChangeReview), and the re-pin merges with them. The loop runs until every layer is current."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:52
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The body that issues the guideline (for example WHO). It publishes a new version with change notes that say what changed and why. It does not decide how a country adapts. That is the adaptation committee&#x27;s call."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:118
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The committee reads the old version, the new version and each affected adaptation side by side on the staging preview, and hears the adaptation team&#x27;s account of what rests on them."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:66
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The country or implementer team that keeps the adaptations: the local content, overlays and overrides that sit on top of the guideline. It reads the impact report, says which adaptations and policies a change touches, and makes the revisions the committee decides."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:79
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The issuing body publishes a new version. A country that adapted an earlier version enters here when it decides to take it up."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:83
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The publisher states what changed, what was added and what was withdrawn, and why, in words a country team can act on. The notes go with the release, so the comparison below starts from the publisher&#x27;s own account rather than only from a diff."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:141
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The re-pin merges when its checks are green and every decision it needs is recorded. Its pull request cites the decisions, which become the release notes for this site&#x27;s update."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:72
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The stakeholders who own the adapted guideline: policy, clinical and programme leads, and others the country names. They review the impact with the old and new versions side by side and decide, for each adaptation, whether to keep, revise or retire it. Their decisions are recorded, and they are what the release notes cite."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/guideline-updates.bpmn:163
#. Diagram label
msgid "yes"
msgstr ""
